m in; then the myth that it cooks from the inside out. The camera opens close on the food in the waves, stays mid on the oven, and ends on the home view.","hold":true},"sentences":[{"role":"hook","text":"If you shine invisible waves at food, you have a microwave oven."},{"role":"problem","text":"But the waves heat one side, and the other side stays cold."},{"role":"fix1","text":"So you add a turntable that spins the food through the waves."},{"role":"problem2","text":"But now the waves leak out of the open front."},{"role":"fix2","text":"So you add a door with a metal mesh whose holes are far smaller than the waves."},{"role":"name","text":"This is a microwave oven."},{"role":"how","text":"The waves shake water in the food 2.45 billion times a second."},{"role":"myth","text":"And it does not cook from the inside out."},{"role":"mythFact","text":"The waves reach just 1 to 1.5 inches, and heat creeps inward inch by inch."},{"role":"finish","text":"Add a keypad, a timer and a light."},{"role":"congrats","text":"Congratulations, you have built a microwave oven."}]}